---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
---
<ToolLayout title="Spreadsheet List Cleaner" category="Office" description="Clean a pasted column, remove duplicate entries or compare two lists. Keep your codes intact and copy the result back to your spreadsheet.">
 <div class="kit-workspace">
  <form class="kit-panel" id="list-form"><div class="kit-row"><h2>1. Add your list</h2><button class="kit-btn" id="list-example" type="button">Try an example</button></div>
   <div class="kit-field"><label for="list-mode">What would you like to do?</label><select id="list-mode"><option value="clean">Clean List A</option><option value="only-a">Find entries only in List A</option><option value="only-b">Find entries only in List B</option><option value="common">Find entries in both lists</option><option value="combine">Combine both lists, without duplicates</option></select></div>
   <div class="kit-field"><label for="list-a">List A — one entry per line</label><textarea id="list-a" maxlength="500000" placeholder="00125&#10;00126&#10;00125" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="list-limit"></textarea></div>
   <div class="kit-field" id="list-b-field" hidden><label for="list-b">List B — one entry per line</label><textarea id="list-b" maxlength="500000" placeholder="00126&#10;00127" spellcheck="false"></textarea></div>
   <div role="group" aria-labelledby="cleaning-options-label"><p id="cleaning-options-label" class="kit-field-label" style="line-height:1.5;padding-top:4px">Cleaning options</p><div class="kit-options"><label><input id="list-trim" type="checkbox" checked/>Trim outer spaces</label><label><input id="list-dedupe" type="checkbox" checked/>Remove duplicates</label><label><input id="list-case" type="checkbox" checked/>Case-sensitive</label><label><input id="list-sort" type="checkbox"/>Sort A–Z</label></div></div>
   <p class="kit-help" id="list-limit">Up to 20,000 rows and 500,000 characters per list. Blank rows are removed. Comparison results contain unique entries.</p>
   <div class="kit-actions"><button class="kit-btn primary" type="submit">Process list →</button><button class="kit-btn" id="list-clear" type="button">Clear all</button></div><p class="kit-status kit-error" id="list-error" role="alert"></p>
  </form>
  <section class="kit-panel kit-result" aria-labelledby="list-result-heading"><h2 id="list-result-heading">2. Your result</h2><p class="kit-help" id="list-summary" role="status">Add a list or try the example to get started.</p><div class="kit-stats"><div><strong id="list-input-count">—</strong><span>Input entries</span></div><div><strong id="list-output-count">—</strong><span>Result entries</span></div><div><strong id="list-duplicate-count">—</strong><span>Duplicates in input</span></div></div><label for="list-result">Ready to copy</label><textarea id="list-result" readonly spellcheck="false" placeholder="Your cleaned list will appear here."></textarea><div class="kit-actions"><button class="kit-btn" id="list-copy" disabled>Copy result</button><button class="kit-btn" id="list-download" disabled>Download .txt</button></div><p class="kit-status" id="list-message" role="status"></p><p class="kit-help">Text download preserves the original characters. In Excel, format the destination column as Text before pasting codes with leading zeros.</p></section>
 </div>
 <p class="kit-note">✓ Your lists are processed in this browser and are not uploaded or saved by this tool.</p>
 <section class="kit-guide" id="guide"><h2>Clean data without changing its meaning.</h2><div class="kit-guide-grid"><div><h3>1. Paste one column</h3><p>Copy a column from Excel or another spreadsheet. Each line becomes an entry. Include the values only, without the column heading.</p></div><div><h3>2. Choose the rules</h3><p>Keep case-sensitive matching on for product codes where “AB” and “ab” are different. Trimming only removes spaces before and after an entry.</p></div><div><h3>3. Take the result</h3><p>Copy the cleaned values or download a text file. Comparisons preserve the spelling from the source list; shared entries use List A’s spelling.</p></div></div>
 <details><summary>Example: compare received stock with a supplier list</summary><p>List A contains 00125, 00126 and 00125. List B contains 00126 and 00127. “Only in List A” returns 00125. “In both lists” returns 00126. These are differences between lists, not proof of missing stock: check your underlying records.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Will this keep leading zeros and commas?</summary><p>Yes. Values are treated as text. “00125” stays “00125” and a comma inside an entry is preserved. This tool is for pasted single columns, not multi-column CSV files. Your spreadsheet can still remove zeros on paste unless the destination is formatted as Text.</p></details>
 <details><summary>What happens to duplicates and blank lines?</summary><p>Blank or whitespace-only lines are removed. The first occurrence is kept when removing duplicates. Comparison modes always use unique entries. The duplicate count counts repeats within each input list; an entry appearing once in both lists is not counted as an input duplicate.</p></details>
 </section>
</ToolLayout>
<script>
import {processLists} from '../../../utils/list-tools.mjs';
import {copyText,downloadText} from '../../../utils/tool-browser';
const get=<T extends HTMLElement>(id:string)=>document.getElementById(id) as T;
const a=get<HTMLTextAreaElement>('list-a'),b=get<HTMLTextAreaElement>('list-b'),mode=get<HTMLSelectElement>('list-mode'),result=get<HTMLTextAreaElement>('list-result');
const copy=get<HTMLButtonElement>('list-copy'),download=get<HTMLButtonElement>('list-download'),error=get('list-error'),message=get('list-message');
function invalidate(){result.value='';copy.disabled=true;download.disabled=true;error.textContent='';message.textContent='';get('list-summary').textContent='Ready when you are. Select Process list to update the result.';['input','output','duplicate'].forEach(key=>get(`list-${key}-count`).textContent='—');}
function syncMode(){get('list-b-field').hidden=mode.value==='clean';get<HTMLInputElement>('list-dedupe').disabled=mode.value!=='clean';invalidate();}
get('list-form').addEventListener('input',invalidate);mode.addEventListener('change',syncMode);
get('list-form').addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();error.textContent='';message.textContent='';try{if(!a.value.trim()&&!b.value.trim())throw new Error('Add at least one entry to a list.');const output=processLists(a.value,b.value,{mode:mode.value,trim:get<HTMLInputElement>('list-trim').checked,caseSensitive:get<HTMLInputElement>('list-case').checked,deduplicate:get<HTMLInputElement>('list-dedupe').checked,sort:get<HTMLInputElement>('list-sort').checked});result.value=output.values.join('\n');get('list-input-count').textContent=output.inputCount.toLocaleString();get('list-output-count').textContent=output.values.length.toLocaleString();get('list-duplicate-count').textContent=output.duplicates.toLocaleString();get('list-summary').textContent=`Done. ${output.values.length.toLocaleString()} result entries. ${output.blanks} blank rows removed.`;copy.disabled=download.disabled=output.values.length===0;}catch(e){invalidate();error.textContent=e instanceof Error?e.message:'Unable to process this list.';}});
get('list-example').addEventListener('click',()=>{a.value=' 00125\n00126\n00125\n\nAB-20\nab-20 ';b.value='00126\n00127\nAB-20';invalidate();});
get('list-clear').addEventListener('click',()=>{a.value='';b.value='';invalidate();a.focus();});
copy.addEventListener('click',()=>copyText(result.value,message));download.addEventListener('click',()=>{downloadText(result.value,'kriyano-list.txt');message.textContent='Text download started.';});
</script>
